8927.1;+557,;10~WP-start~15
SYMPTOM/SYNDROME						  POTENTIAL PATHOGENS 		PRECAUTIONS
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Reported recent history of MDRO					  MRSA, VRE, ESBL, CRE, 	Contact or Enhanced Barrier (CLC)
								  C. auris 
Acute diarrhea w/recent history of healthcare or antibiotics 	  C. difficile   		Contact Plus
Acute diarrhea w/nausea/vomiting   				  Norovirus      		Contact Plus
Fever + Headache, stiff neck, photophobia	   		  N. Meningitis     		Droplet
Fever + Rash					    		  Measles, Chickenpox	  	Airborne/Contact
Fever + (cough,sore throat,rhinorrhea,myalgia,headache,fatigue)   Influenza			Droplet
   *Presence of ANY of these OR loss of taste or smell   	  COVID         		Droplet/Contact + Eye Protection
    may prompt consideration for COVID	
Fever + cough + (hemoptysis, night sweats, weight loss) 	  TB				Airborne
Abscess or draining wound that can't be covered			  MRSA, MSSA, GAS    		Contact

Contact Infection Prevention and Control Specialist if patient placed in isolation for confirmation of isolation type
]]>
</FILEMAN_FDA>
